# --- Environment -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Jupyter ---------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Data -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The nine raw Olist CSVs ARE committed (126 MB) so the repository is
# self-contained: anyone can clone it and reproduce the notebooks, the figures
# and the deployed dashboard without hunting for the source files. The largest,
# geolocation at 61 MB, is under GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# The 108 MB SQLite build of the same data is redundant with the CSVs and does
# exceed that limit, so it stays out.
IT5006_Project-Data/

# Derived data is regenerated from the CSVs on demand and is not tracked.
data/processed/

# --- Course materials, not ours to redistribute ----------------------------
# The assignment brief, the reference PDFs and the sample reports were provided
# by the course.
/broadway_clean.csv
/phase 1 requirements.docx
/phase 2 requirements.docx
/phase1_req_dump.txt
/NIBRS_DataDictionary.pdf
/nibrs_diagram.pdf
sample reports (for reference only)/

# --- Report -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1 kept the LaTeX sources out of the repository and tracked only the
# compiled PDF. Phase 2 reverses that: report/ now holds the .tex, the section
# files and refs.bib, so the whole folder uploads to Overleaf and compiles as-is,
# and so the three of us can edit one copy rather than mail it around. The
# generated stats files are tracked too - they are what the manuscript is diffed
# against, and a reader should be able to check a number without running
# anything.
#
# Build artefacts stay out.

# LaTeX build artefacts
report/*.aux
report/*.bbl
report/*.blg
report/*.log
report/*.out
report/*.toc
report/*.synctex.gz
report/*.fls
report/*.fdb_latexmk

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
